{
  "id": "iteriodev-turnview",
  "kind": "tool",
  "version": "0.11.0",
  "title": "Turn View",
  "description": "The front camera in the instrument cluster with a turn card and, near each turn, a blue turn sign (three chevrons pointing the way), from BMW navigation, CarPlay or Android Auto; the camera alone without a route. Or on the head unit instead (0.9.0, the Turn View app's Camera page: Picture on Head unit), at any speed: the camera's whole picture with the same card and sign, a kerb-parking aid. iDrive 8: pick \"Turn View AR\" in the cluster widget menu (from the car's next start after installing). iDrive 7: off at every start of the car; switch it on in the Turn View app and set Instrument cluster > Central display area to Map view; the camera takes the map area there. 0.11.0: iDrive 7 with the IterioDev cluster design: pick Turn View with the BC button in the design's centre widget (opt-in in the cluster design app) and switch Turn View on in its app; the camera then shows in that widget. Not together with Waze on cluster on the cluster: set Waze on cluster to HUD only (the cluster and the HUD show 2 videos at most). 0.10.0: on cars with BMW Night Vision, its picture instead of the front camera (the Turn View app's Camera page: Camera Night Vision), read from the head unit's own video input - BMW's Night Vision screen then stays black. Set up and calibrated in the Turn View app. Drawn by Cluster renderer (robertnisipeanu/idrive-apps) 0.5.10 or newer. No coding needed.",
  "optional": true,
  "uninstallable": true,
  "mguHmi": [
    "ID7",
    "ID8"
  ],
  "requires": {
    "cluster-render": "0.5.10",
    "mgu-deploy": "0.7.11"
  },
